  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14195525/assets/ab0416aeff61e4916acc1765a7931da0a41a64ba9d0ac4c05a322de6a1ed431b.png)\n\nA box whose depth $z$ is equal to half of its height $y$ has a manufacturing cost that depends on two materials. The material for the top and bottom costs $$4$ per square meter, and the material for the lateral faces costs $$1$ per square meter. The box must have a volume of $36\\,{m}^{3}.$\n\nWhat is the value of $z$ for the box that has the smallest production cost? Do not round the answer.\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}} units",
